    <\associate|figure>
      <tuple|normal|<surround|<hidden-binding|<tuple>|4.1>||The field at
      resolution <with|mode|<quote|math>|t>,
      <with|mode|<quote|math>|X<rsub|t>>, for the heat profile on
      <with|mode|<quote|math>|\<bbb-T\><rsup|2>>
      (<with|mode|<quote|math>|m=4>, mean subtracted for display), at
      <with|mode|<quote|math>|t=8,32,128> and at the lattice cutoff, all
      built from the same white noise. The martingale
      <with|mode|<quote|math>|X<rsub|t>> reveals finer and finer details,
      while the large scales are fixed at low resolution.>|<pageref|auto-8>>

      <tuple|normal|<surround|<hidden-binding|<tuple>|5.1>||The
      forward\Ubackward structure of <with|font-shape|<quote|right>|(<reference|eq:fbsde-system>)>
      on <with|mode|<quote|math>|\<bbb-T\><rsup|2>>, heat profile, at
      resolutions <with|mode|<quote|math>|t<rsub|1>\<less\>t<rsub|2>\<less\>t<rsub|3>\<less\>T>,
      all built from the same noise. Top: the field gains the fluctuation of
      each shell, <with|mode|<quote|math>|<wide|Q|\<dot\>><rsub|t><rsup|1/2>\<mathd\>W<rsub|t>>,
      and reveals finer modes. Bottom: the effective force
      <with|mode|<quote|math>|F<rsub|t>=\<bbb-E\><rsub|t>*<around|[|-D*V<rsub|T><around|(|\<Phi\><rsub|T>|)>|]>>
      for the <with|mode|<quote|math>|\<Phi\><rsup|4>> interaction,
      determined backward from the terminal interaction. It is shown to first
      order in <with|mode|<quote|math>|\<lambda\>>, where it is the Wick cube
      <with|mode|<quote|math>|-4*\<lambda\>*H<rsub|3>*<around|(|\<Phi\><rsub|t>;c<rsub|t>|)>>,
      and each panel is in its own units.>|<pageref|auto-14>>

      <tuple|normal|<surround|<hidden-binding|<tuple>|5.2>||A
      zero-dimensional Polchinski process (Exercise
      <no-break><specific|screen|<resize|<move|<with|color|<quote|#A0A0FF>|->|-0.3em|>|0em||0em|>><reference|ex:zero-dim>):
      <with|mode|<quote|math>|Q<rsub|t>=1-\<mathe\><rsup|-t>>,
      <with|mode|<quote|math>|T=5>, <with|mode|<quote|math>|V<rsub|T><around|(|x|)>=<frac|1|2>*x<rsup|4>-<frac|3|2>*x<rsup|2>>.
      Left: the effective force <with|mode|<quote|math>|F<rsub|t>=-V<rsub|t><rprime|'>>
      is almost linear at low resolution and develops the double-well
      structure as <with|mode|<quote|math>|t\<to\>T>. Centre: paths of the
      FBSDE <with|font-shape|<quote|right>|(<reference|eq:fbsde>)>, which
      split between the two wells (stochastic localisation). Right: histogram
      of <with|mode|<quote|math>|\<Phi\><rsub|T>>
      (<with|mode|<quote|math>|2\<cdot\>10<rsup|4>> paths) against the
      density of <with|mode|<quote|math>|\<nu\><rsub|T>>.>|<pageref|auto-15>>

      <tuple|normal|<surround|<hidden-binding|<tuple>|6.1>||Stochastic
      localisation for a two-component field:
      <with|mode|<quote|math>|Q<rsub|t>=<around|(|1-\<mathe\><rsup|-t>|)>*<with|math-font|<quote|Bbb>|1>>,
      <with|mode|<quote|math>|T=4>, <with|mode|<quote|math>|V<rsub|T>> a
      tilted double well, and the contours show the density of
      <with|mode|<quote|math>|\<nu\><rsub|T>>. One path of
      <with|font-shape|<quote|right>|(<reference|eq:fbsde>)> up to resolution
      <with|mode|<quote|math>|t> (navy), with its terminal value
      <with|mode|<quote|math>|\<Phi\><rsub|T>> (open circle). The forecast
      <with|mode|<quote|math>|\<psi\><rsub|t>=\<Phi\><rsub|t>+S<rsub|t>*F<rsub|t>>
      (gold) is the mean of the conditional law
      <with|mode|<quote|math>|\<mu\><rsub|t><rsup|\<Phi\><rsub|t>>>: teal
      samples, and the ellipse is two standard deviations of
      <with|mode|<quote|math>|<with|mode|<quote|text>|<with|font-family|<quote|rm>|font-shape|<quote|right>|Cov>><rsub|t>>.
      At low resolution the conditional law covers both wells; as
      <with|mode|<quote|math>|t> grows it localises on one of
      them.>|<pageref|auto-25>>

      <tuple|normal|<surround|<hidden-binding|<tuple>|6.2>||The
      zero-dimensional model of Figure <no-break><specific|screen|<resize|<move|<with|color|<quote|#A0A0FF>|->|-0.3em|>|0em||0em|>><reference|fig:polchinski-0d>
      at <with|mode|<quote|math>|t=1.2>. Left: the shear
      <with|mode|<quote|math>|\<Sigma\><rsub|t>> (teal arrows) maps the graph
      of the force <with|mode|<quote|math>|F<rsub|t>=-V<rsub|t><rprime|'>>
      (navy) to a graph over the forecast <with|mode|<quote|math>|\<psi\>>
      (gold), which is the graph of <with|mode|<quote|math>|-\<Gamma\><rsub|t><rprime|'>>.
      Right: the bare potential <with|mode|<quote|math>|V<rsub|T>>, the
      effective potential <with|mode|<quote|math>|V<rsub|t>> and
      <with|mode|<quote|math>|\<Gamma\><rsub|t>>, each shifted to have
      minimum <with|mode|<quote|math>|0>.>|<pageref|auto-27>>

      <tuple|normal|<surround|<hidden-binding|<tuple>|6.3>||The regulator
      <with|mode|<quote|math>|<with|math-font|<quote|cal*>|R><rsub|t>> of the
      heat profile (<with|mode|<quote|math>|T=\<infty\>>,
      <with|mode|<quote|math>|m=1>): close to the mass term
      <with|mode|<quote|math>|t<rsup|2>> (dotted) on the modes
      <with|mode|<quote|math>|<around|\||k|\|>\<ll\>t>, exponentially small
      on the modes <with|mode|<quote|math>|<around|\||k|\|>\<gg\>t>.>|<pageref|auto-28>>

      <tuple|normal|<surround|<hidden-binding|<tuple>|8.1>||Covariation of
      point observables, heat profile in <with|mode|<quote|math>|d=2>. Left:
      the kernels of <with|mode|<quote|math>|<wide|Q|\<dot\>><rsub|s><rsup|1/2>>
      centred at <with|mode|<quote|math>|x> (navy) and at
      <with|mode|<quote|math>|y> (teal) at three resolutions, with their
      overlap (gold). The integral of the product of the two kernels is the
      covariation density <with|mode|<quote|math>|<wide|Q|\<dot\>><rsub|s>*<around|(|x-y|)>>.
      Right: <with|mode|<quote|math>|s\<mapsto\><wide|Q|\<dot\>><rsub|s>*<around|(|x-y|)>>
      for three distances (<with|mode|<quote|math>|m=1>). Its integral is
      <with|mode|<quote|math>|G*<around|(|x-y|)>>, and it is negligible for
      <with|mode|<quote|math>|s\<gg\>1/<around|\||x-y|\|>>. As
      <with|mode|<quote|math>|y\<to\>x> the mass moves to
      <with|mode|<quote|math>|s\<to\>\<infty\>>, which is the divergence of
      the product at coincident points.>|<pageref|auto-50>>
